# 16. Viewsets | gs10

    # - ViewSet : it will automatically create all the CRUD operations based on the methods defined in the viewset class


    # 1) Viewset-class : we have to define all the methods for CRUD operations in the viewset class
        # - list(self, request) : for GET request to get all the records
        # - create(self, request) : for POST request to create a new record
        # - retrieve(self, request, pk=None) : for GET request to get a single record based on the primary key
        # - update(self, request, pk=None) : for PUT request to update a record based on the primary key
        # - partial_update(self, request, pk=None) : for PATCH request to update a record based on the primary key
        # - destroy(self, request, pk=None) : for DELETE request to delete a record based on the primary key


        # Attributes :

        # most used attributes in viewset class are :
        # - basename
        # - action
        # - detail
        # - suffix
        # - name
        # - description

        # least used attributes in viewset class are :
        # - queryset
        # - serializer_class
        # - lookup_field
        # - lookup_url_kwargs
        # - http_method_names
        # - renderer_classes
        # - filter_backends
        # - pagination_class

        # - normal and primary key based url are automatically generated by the router based on the methods defined in the viewset class and the basename provided in the router.register() method.

        # - all create, read, update and delete operations are automatically generated by the router.

# 17. 2) ModelViewSet : it will automatically create all the CRUD operations based on the queryset and serializer_class defined in the viewset class

        # - queryset : it is used to define the queryset for the viewset class
        # - serializer_class : it is used to define the serializer class for the viewset class
        # - all create, read, update and delete operations are automatically generated by the router based on the queryset and serializer_class defined in the viewset class.


